  "source": "[\\group.element:of{G}]\nDeclares: x is \\monoid.element:of{G}\nwhen: G is \\group\nEnables:\n. capability: x.inv :=> \\group.inverse:of{x}:in{G}\n  written: \"x+?^{-1}\"\nDocumented:\n. called: \"element of group $G?$\"\n. description: \"An element of a group is a member of its underlying set. Because\n                the ambient structure is a group, each such element $x$ has a\n                well-defined inverse $x^{-1}$, accessible through its inverse\n                operation.\"\nId: \"858abdda-c416-4a4e-a0bf-27ecf84cf008\"",
